  the public domain.
  Ends at "y danos tu gozo eterno." with no "Amén", as in the Lectionary.

Salmos 16, 23, 27, 51, 84 and 136
  "La Biblia. El Libro del Pueblo de Dios" (traducción argentina), as the
  Holy See's site publishes it:
    Salmo 16   https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PGL.HTM
    Salmo 23   https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PGS.HTM
    Salmo 27   https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PGW.HTM
    Salmo 51   https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PHK.HTM
    Salmo 84   https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PIH.HTM
    Salmo 136  https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PJX.HTM
  Copyright © Libreria Editrice Vaticana
  Used with attribution; all rights remain with the publisher.
  The psalms follow the source's Hebrew numbering. Their superscriptions and
  the verse numbers are left out. Kept exactly as printed: "la Muerte"
  (Ps 16), "Señor del Universo" (Ps 84, 2), "¡Aleluya!" at the start of
  Ps 136 and "Dios de los Dioses" (Ps 136, 2).

Bienaventuranzas (Mateo 5, 3-12), Himno al amor (1 Corintios 13, 1-13) and
Prólogo de san Juan (Juan 1, 1-18)
  "La Biblia. El Libro del Pueblo de Dios" (traducción argentina), as the
  Holy See's site publishes it:
    Mateo 5         https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PUF.HTM
    1 Corintios 13  https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PYC.HTM
    Juan 1          https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PW7.HTM
  Copyright © Libreria Editrice Vaticana
  Used with attribution; all rights remain with the publisher.
  Verse numbers are left out. The Beatitudes drop the opening guillemet of
  Mt 5, 3, since the speech goes on past v. 12. The Prologue keeps "El no era
  luz" (Jn 1, 8) as printed. Two transcription typos of the 1 Corintios page
  are corrected, as the Bible reads:
    1 Cor 13, 5   "no tienen en cuenta el mal recibido" is given as
                  "no tiene en cuenta el mal recibido"
    1 Cor 13, 13  "la más grande todas es el amor" is given as
                  "la más grande de todas es el amor"

Magníficat (Lucas 1, 46-55)
  "La Biblia. El Libro del Pueblo de Dios" (traducción argentina), as the
  Holy See's site publishes it.
  Copied from https://www.vatican.va/archive/ESL0506/__PVJ.HTM
  Copyright © Libreria Editrice Vaticana
  Used with attribution; all rights remain with the publisher.
  The text starts at «Mi alma canta» (the narrative "María dijo entonces:" is
  left out) and the verse numbers are left out. Two transcription typos of
  the page are corrected, as the Bible reads:
    Lc 1, 48  "porque el miró" is given as "porque él miró"
    Lc 1, 49  "el Todopoderoso he hecho" is given as "el Todopoderoso ha hecho"

